{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And blessed be El Elyon.</b> This act that He performed — granting Abraham victory over his enemies — is a blessing to Him, may He be blessed, for in it He rejoices in His deeds: in the destruction of the wicked and the triumph of the righteous, as it says: שַׁבְּחוּהוּ כָּל הָאוֹמִּים כִּי גָבַר עָלֵינוּ חַסְדּוֹ (Psalms 117:1–2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:08.230460371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}